;; The files of repr/python's round trip (bin/repr-python roundtrip; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: PY2")
;; that do not pass every level, by corpus, each with its class (:classes, each with what it is and the decision
;; it rests on). Written by bin/repr-python roundtrip --record, the classes kept; the writer classes a file only by
;; rule (:rejected, :code-lines) and never writes a guess: a file of no class makes the run exit 3. Read with the
;; Clojure reader.
{:classes
 {:code-lines
  {:decided "by definition: compile() is a function of the ast with its positions, so with the ast equal the difference is the positions'; :full (PY3) keeps them", :what "levels 1 and 2 pass (the forms and the ast without positions are equal) but the code compiled from the print differs from the original's after the normalization of tools/pydump's code_digest: CPython 3.14's code generation depends on the lines a node spans beyond what the normalization removes (where an exception range or a jump falls), and :lines carries no lines"}
  :rejected
  {:decided "the survey's §5.3 (PYS3 (a)): the read level's reference is CPython's acceptance and message", :what "CPython's ast.parse rejects the file (a deliberately bad file of Lib/test: an unknown or wrong encoding, a character no identifier takes): the read gives (python/error CLASS MSG ...), judged on CPython's class and message (survey §5.3); nothing to print"}}
